{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>The hidden things.</b> Because he said above: 'and he blesses himself in his heart' — and by reasoning, he does it in secret." "<b>To YHWH our Elohim.</b> The matter is upon Him, since He exacts punishment from those who transgress in secret." "<b>And the revealed things.</b> And the revealed transgressions depend on us and on our children, if we do not remove the evil from our midst. And since you should not say this measure applies forever, there are points over <b>לנו ולבנינו</b> ('to us and to our children'), to say that once they crossed the Jordan and accepted the Torah and became guarantors for one another, even <b>the hidden things are לנו ולבנינו</b>. And if you ask: if so, since we would be excluding hidden things from 'לה׳ אלהינו,' he should have placed points over 'ה׳ אלהינו' — one may answer: it is not customary to place points over it, because it would appear as erasure. And since the points of לנו ולבנינו stand in place of the points he should have placed over the (name of) HaShem, the ayin of עד was also dotted, so as to complete the number of letters in לה׳ אלהינו. It is fitting to ask why Rashi did not explain here the point on the ayin of עד." "<b>The hidden things to YHWH our Elohim.</b> Concerning this it is said: 'And of them too I shall take for the priests and for the Levites,' etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {2 "In the phrase 'over the (name of) HaShem,' the Hebrew says על ה׳ — HaShem referring to the divine name YHWH just quoted; rendered as 'the (name of) HaShem' to clarify that the points would have been placed over the divine name itself.", 3 "The verse cited (Isaiah 66:21) is linked because 'hidden' (נסתרות) shares a root with the Levitical cities of refuge and concealment, per rabbinic tradition connecting this phrase to priestly/Levitical selection."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:51.069685112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}